7.2   ADE singularities and the McKay correspondence (proved)

The classification of F by Whitney singularities A1 → A2 → A3 matches the ADE singularity
classification governing gauge groups in orbifold compactifications C2 /Γ via the McKay correspon-
dence [4]. The McKay correspondence is a theorem in algebraic geometry:

Theorem 7.1 (McKay, 1980 [4]). There is a bijection between the non-trivial irreducible represen-
tations of a finite subgroup Γ ⊂ SU(2) and the nodes of the corresponding Dynkin diagram of type
A, D, or E. The An series corresponds to the cyclic group Zn+1 , whose associated gauge group is
SU(n + 1).

In particular: A1 ↔ SU(2), A2 ↔ SU(3) (QCD gauge group), A3 ↔ SU(4).


7.3   T-duality fixed point (proved)

Theorem 7.2 (Buscher, 1987 [5]). The bosonic string compactified on a circle of radius R (in α ′ = 1
units) is equivalent to the string compactified on a circle of radius 1/R. The fixed point of this
R ↔ 1/R duality is R = 1. The corresponding period is T ∗ = 2πR = 2π.

The dm3 limit cycle has period T ∗ = 2π (one full rotation of θ per unit z-advance). Identification
(conjectured): the dm3 invariant T ∗ = 2π is the T-self-dual radius R = 1.
Figure 3 shows the three-scale operator chain.



